<title>USA: Microelectronic Packaging names new CFO.</title>
<headline>Microelectronic Packaging names new CFO.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Microelectronic Packaging Inc said Tuesday it has named Denis Trafecanty as its new chief financial officer, succeeding David Hinkle, who left the CFO position in April.</p>
<p>Trafecanty, 53, has more than two decades of executive financial experience, having held CFO positions at major computer, electronic and television companies, the company said.</p>
<p>Most recently, he was CFO at the Tandon Group of companies since 1984.</p>
